The first is an [unnecessary/incorrect reportOverlappingOverload](https://pyright-play.net/?code=GYJw9gtgBALgngBwJYDsDmUkQWEMoAUAUFKVAIIpwA0JZAwgIYA2zjARswKa1lT1gUAY0YwuKUTzqkACoxCMIAZQRchvMgBVEXAGryNpMADcuIZmEYATWgEoiRGVAC8UOQuWqhBAEQyf9gBCYACuKFZOru6KKmq%2BwWERAUQASi5Q2qr6IL4pyUrpmXryvkrJDgACJmYW1kRWXMBQDUK4orgEwABc-CxsnFwA2gLCkhJig-Cqg0oAutRu81Aps7ZQALQAfJgoMD0AdIdEVabmllb1jc1qbTAd0lDdvawc3MOCImLjQ0oLMksrIhrLY7PZQQ77Y7VM51BpNFq3e58J5MF4DQYyBaA4HbVBgiGXeE3BR3HJPShwHGgroPEBcGAhEAoKAARiIQA). These overloads aren't overlapping and Pyright selects the correct one, but it reports them as overlapping.
