`P0` is a runtime-checkable protocol. `P1` is also a runtime-checkable protocol and it inherits `P0`. Variable `x` is typed as `P0`. When `x` is type-narrowed as `P1`, its type is incorrectly recognized as `Never` instead of `P1`.

Only occurs when `P1` is a protocol, but not when `P1` is a normal class.

